@copilot Update this PR directly with one scoped correction to the new MySQL reproducer's Gradle wiring. The completed Copilot review at https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20941#discussion_r4368052017 correctly identifies that the new usesService(testcontainersBuildService) registration in instrumentation/jdbc/javaagent/build.gradle.kts currently applies to every Test task. The shared service allows only two concurrent users, so container-free tasks now unnecessarily consume its slots.

Scope this registration to the test tasks that actually include MySqlReplicationTest, preserving it for all applicable normal, preview-semconv, exception-signal, and dependency-test variants. Do not register the container-free testSlick, testSqlCommenter, testCaptureParameters, or testTransactions tasks. Follow existing Gradle task-configuration patterns rather than adding an elaborate task-inspection mechanism. Preserve the existing testLatestDeps system property on all Test tasks.

Keep the production DbInfo cache fix, configured logical server.address behavior, MySQL routing reproducer, and fallback coverage unchanged. Run the narrowest formatting and relevant validation for this Gradle correction and record the results in task evidence. Do not merge, create another PR, or reply to or resolve review threads; this coordinator handles review-thread disposition.

