@copilot Update this PR directly with a comment-only clarification in instrumentation/jdbc/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/jdbc/DriverInstrumentation.java.

Replace the comment "// Multi-host drivers may expose the unwrapped connection through their statements." with this agreed wording:

```java
// Query instrumentation looks up DbInfo after unwrapping the connection,
// which can return a different object than Driver.connect() returned.
// On a cache miss, it parses connection.getMetaData().getURL(). For MySQL
// replication, that URL can contain an internally generated identifier
// instead of the configured hosts. Cache the original URL's DbInfo on
// the unwrapped object too, so query instrumentation finds it there.
```

Keep the executable code, tests, dependency pins, base, and draft state unchanged. This is only a clarification of the later cache lookup and metadata fallback, not a request to change wrapper handling. Do not restore the intentionally removed decorator guard or test. Use normal module formatting if needed; no behavior tests or unrelated validation are needed for this comment-only edit. Commit and push the change to this PR's existing branch. Do not create another PR, merge, post replies, or resolve threads. The coordinator handles metadata and thread disposition.

